  "post": {
    "caption": "Cartier's square watch honors a pilot. Cartier says Louis Cartier made it for his pilot friend, the Brazilian aviator Alberto Santos Dumont, and dates that story to 1904. Checking a pocket watch while flying was awkward, so Cartier made him one for his wrist. Its case was square, when most watches were round, and the bezel shows off its screws. In 1911 it went on sale to everyone, made with help from the watchmaker Edmond Jaeger, in platinum and yellow gold. In 1978 it came back as the Santos de Cartier.",
